{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences of length 12 over {0,1} with no run of 3 consecutive same bits. Classic combinatorial: count binary strings with no 3 consecutive equal bits. This is Fibonacci-like. Let a_n be number of valid strings length n. We can use recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}. Wait need to consider last run length. Let's define states: ending with run of length 1 of 0 or 1, or run of length 2. Let's define:\n\nLet A_n = number of valid strings length n ending with a single 0 (i.e., last bit 0, previous bit not 0 or doesn't exist). Similarly B_n ending with single 1. C_n ending with double 0 (i.e., last two bits 00). D_n ending with double 1 (11). Then recurrence:\n\nA_{n} = B_{n-1} + D_{n-1} (since to end with single 0, previous must be 1, either single or double). Similarly B_n = A_{n-1} + C_{n-1}.\n\nC_n = A_{n-1} (to have 00, previous must be single 0). D_n = B_{n-1}.\n\nBase n=1: strings of length1: \"0\" and \"1\". So A_1=1, B_1=1, C_1=0, D_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=12.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=1,B=1,C=0,D=0. total a1=2.\n\nn=2:\nA2 = B1 + D1 =1+0=1\nB2 = A1 + C1 =1+0=1\nC2 = A1 =1\nD2 = B1 =1\ntotal =1+1+1+1=4. (All 4 strings length2 allowed)\n\nn=3:\nA3 = B2 + D2 =1+1=2\nB3 = A2 + C2 =1+1=2\nC3 = A2 =1\nD3 = B2 =1\ntotal=2+2+1+1=6. (All 8 minus 2 with 000 or 111? Actually length3 strings: 000,001,010,011,100,101,110,111. Forbidden: 000,111. So 6 valid. matches.)\n\nn=4:\nA4 = B3 + D3 =2+1=3\nB4 = A3 + C3 =2+1=3\nC4 = A3 =2\nD4 = B3 =2\ntotal=3+3+2+2=10.\n\nn=5:\nA5 = B4 + D4 =3+2=5\nB5 = A4 + C4 =3+2=5\nC5 = A4 =3\nD5 = B4 =3\ntotal=5+5+3+3=16.\n\nn=6:\nA6 = B5 + D5 =5+3=8\nB6 = A5 + C5 =5+3=8\nC6 = A5 =5\nD6 = B5 =5\ntotal=8+8+5+5=26.\n\nn=7:\nA7 = B6 + D6 =8+5=13\nB7 = A6 + C6 =8+"}}],"created":1790937733,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10